---
pagination:
  data: sites.compatRoutes
  size: 1
  alias: route
permalink: "/api/{{ route.hash }}.json"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#
  Compatibility route for the original Speedlify's API.

  The documented, preferred usage of `<speedlify-score>` hardcodes a hash in the
  markup, so pages we do not control request this filename directly. It is the
  one route whose absence breaks an embed that is already deployed.

  Only the four Lighthouse scores are emitted, because they are the only fields
  whose absence produces a broken render: with no attributes the component shows
  exactly these. Everything else it reads — weight.summary, ranks.cumulative,
  previousRanks.cumulative — sits behind an opt-in attribute and a guard, and
  renders nothing at all when missing rather than failing.

  Sites with no successful measurement emit an empty object: the component
  reads through optional chaining, so it draws nothing instead of erroring.

  Paginated over `compatRoutes` rather than over entries, because one site can
  answer to more than one of these filenames: the hash is computed over the URL
  as a config wrote it, and a trailing slash we normalize away changes it.
-#}
{% if route.lighthouse -%}
{
  "lighthouse": {
    "performance": {{ route.lighthouse.performance | dump | safe }},
    "accessibility": {{ route.lighthouse.accessibility | dump | safe }},
    "bestPractices": {{ route.lighthouse.bestPractices | dump | safe }},
    "seo": {{ route.lighthouse.seo | dump | safe }}
  }
}
{%- else -%}
{}
{%- endif %}
